1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software" means the Cortex platform, including all source code, object code,
   compiled binaries, APIs, database schemas, graph models, scoring algorithms,
   analytics engines, scripts, configuration files, documentation, user manuals,
   and any updates, patches, or enhancements provided by Licensor.

   "License Key" means the unique cryptographic key issued by Licensor to
   Licensee that activates and validates the Software for authorized use.

   "HWID" (Hardware Identifier) means the machine-specific signature generated
   by the Software to bind the license to a designated deployment environment.

   "Deployment Environment" means the specific cloud infrastructure (AWS VPC,
   GCP Project, Azure Subscription) or on-premise server(s) authorized by
   Licensor for Licensee's use of the Software.

   "Knowledge Graph" means the proprietary Neo4j-based property graph database
   constructed by the Software from Licensee's engineering telemetry.

   "Authorized Users" means employees or contractors of Licensee who are
   permitted to access the Software under the applicable subscription tier.

