5. LICENSE VALIDATION & TECHNICAL ENFORCEMENT

   a. The Software incorporates technological protection measures designed to
      prevent unlicensed or unauthorized use. The Software connects periodically
      to Licensor's license verification infrastructure (including the
      cortex-admin control plane) to confirm the validity of the License Key,
      HWID binding, and subscription term.

   b. The Software may operate in a limited offline grace period (up to 14
      calendar days) if connectivity to the license server is temporarily
      unavailable. Beyond this grace period, the Software will restrict
      functionality until license verification is restored.

   c. If the License Key is determined to be invalid, expired, revoked, or
      tampered with, the Software may automatically restrict functionality,
      disable access, or cease operating entirely — without prior notice to
      Licensee.

   d. Licensee acknowledges that any attempt to bypass, spoof, or tamper with
      the license verification system constitutes a material breach of this
      Agreement and may result in immediate termination, legal action, and
      claims for damages.

